10
00:01:04.418 --> 00:01:05.418
Good.

11
00:01:09.418 --> 00:01:24.418
Last week I said that I would give two sermons, two teachings about reflections I had while I was relaxing.

12
00:01:26.418 --> 00:01:30.418
By a crystal-clear lake in southern Europe.

13
00:01:30.418 --> 00:01:31.418
And it was nice.

14
00:01:32.418 --> 00:01:38.418
And what I already explained is that when you come to rest, you can think calmly.

15
00:01:39.418 --> 00:01:49.418
When you are working hard, you are pushing forward, you can take action, you can improvise in life, you can switch gears when necessary, you get into a good flow.

16
00:01:50.418 --> 00:01:54.418
But when you come to rest, you can think calmly, everything relaxed.

17
00:01:55.418 --> 00:02:03.418
And I was able to reflect on two things during my vacation about that.

18
00:02:04.418 --> 00:02:07.418
And I have made two pieces of teaching from that.

19
00:02:08.418 --> 00:02:12.418
Last week I spoke about the unity in God's kingdom.

20
00:02:13.418 --> 00:02:29.418
And I did that based on the fact that I visited a Catholic church five times during those three weeks to be able to glorify God together with my brothers and sisters in the Christian faith.

21
00:02:29.418 --> 00:02:32.418
And it was amazing.

22
00:02:33.418 --> 00:02:37.418
And last week I spoke about unity in God's kingdom.

23
00:02:38.418 --> 00:02:52.418
That it doesn't matter whether you have some kind of title, whether you were raised Catholic or Protestant or Jewish-Messianic or Orthodox or Evangelical.

24
00:02:53.418 --> 00:02:58.418
And I could name another 88,000 denominations, which would tire you out.

25
00:02:59.418 --> 00:03:01.418
And you know, it does matter.

26
00:03:02.418 --> 00:03:05.418
I want to give a disclaimer, I received a lot of responses last week.

27
00:03:06.418 --> 00:03:14.418
And those responses were mainly from people saying, I also had, I also have that desire for the church to be one.

28
00:03:15.418 --> 00:03:16.418
So it's great that it resonates.

29
00:03:16.418 --> 00:03:24.418
But you also get responses, you get responses like, yeah but, do you know how bad the Catholic Church is?

30
00:03:25.418 --> 00:03:28.418
To which my answer is, yes, I know.

31
00:03:29.418 --> 00:03:31.418
But that was not the sermon I gave.

32
00:03:32.418 --> 00:03:39.418
The sermon I gave was that God loves those people who also believe in Jesus.

33
00:03:40.418 --> 00:03:41.418
Who have also accepted Him.

34
00:03:41.418 --> 00:03:43.418
And then it doesn't matter.

35
00:03:44.418 --> 00:03:51.418
And then it does matter, because you have false teachings, you have wrong practices, you have traditions that make no sense.

36
00:03:52.418 --> 00:03:55.418
But what I explained last week, or what I also want to say now.

37
00:03:56.418 --> 00:04:02.418
Suppose I had made a bullet point list to say how bad the Catholic Church was, you would have had a completely different sermon.

38
00:04:03.418 --> 00:04:05.418
Then you would have had an accusatory sermon.

39
00:04:06.418 --> 00:04:10.418
And if I had listed the faults of the Catholic Church, then 30 minutes would not have been enough.

40
00:04:11.418 --> 00:04:14.418
I know, because a lot goes wrong there.

41
00:04:15.418 --> 00:04:23.418
But, if I had made a list of the mistakes that the evangelical church makes, this kind of church, then we would also need a few hours.

42
00:04:24.418 --> 00:04:26.418
And then we would also sit on our knees crying.

43
00:04:27.418 --> 00:04:33.418
And to prevent us from becoming discouraged by the church we attend, we have hope in Christ.

44
00:04:34.418 --> 00:04:39.418
Hallelujah, hallelujah, we are not going to sit and watch each other's fuss, we are going to look at Jesus.

45
00:04:39.418 --> 00:04:40.418
And so it is.

46
00:04:41.418 --> 00:04:51.418
And of course, the Bible is full of warnings that you need to pay attention, I think of the three letters of John, you need to be careful against false teachings.

47
00:04:52.418 --> 00:04:55.418
For false teachings can take you away from the love of Jesus.

48
00:04:56.418 --> 00:05:02.418
The basis of a false teaching is that it no longer recognizes Jesus and that it takes you away from the love of Jesus.

49
00:05:02.418 --> 00:05:27.418
But as long as Jesus is still preached as the risen Lord, who died for you on a cross, He is the King of Kings, born of the virgin Mary, He is the Creator of heaven and earth, He went to the cross for you, He rose from the dead, there is no name but the name of Jesus, He will return to judge the living and the dead, that is a Christian.

50
00:05:28.418 --> 00:05:34.418
And I love Christians, wherever they are, even in Italy, with a nun who is 1 meter 1.

51
00:05:35.418 --> 00:05:47.418
Yes, I still had to think of her this week, and by the way, I once said something to her and I said like this, yes, I really like it here, I don't speak Italian, but hello there, I really like it here.

52
00:05:47.418 --> 00:05:58.418
And she said like this, yes, I don't speak Italian, but hello there, I really like it here, I don't speak Italian, but hello there, I really like it here.

53
00:06:17.418 --> 00:06:25.418
...about how important it is that we talk about this in the church, who knows what topic I will address today, because I have said it.

54
00:06:27.418 --> 00:06:35.418
Food, yes, food, my great hobby, food, hallelujah. Anyone else have a hobby like food?

55
00:06:36.418 --> 00:06:38.418
There are far too few.

56
00:06:39.418 --> 00:06:40.418
Okay.

57
00:06:41.418 --> 00:06:42.418
Okay.

58
00:06:42.418 --> 00:07:00.418
I know, at the end of my previous sermon, I also prayed for all of us, that you would feel the weight of the Holy Spirit in your life, that you would learn what a certain ministry is for your life.

59
00:07:00.418 --> 00:07:12.418
Can you still remember that? That you would experience a certain burden of prayer, something that is a strong opinion in faith, in the Bible, something that you are really moved by.

60
00:07:13.418 --> 00:07:18.418
Something that even takes your emotions with it, that you really think, yes, this really concerns me.

61
00:07:18.418 --> 00:07:32.418
Here I can really cry about this, for example, or here I really get very angry when I see some kind of injustice, or something that has really weighed on your feelings for years, where you truly stand, biblically speaking of course.

62
00:07:33.418 --> 00:07:49.418
Last week I spoke a closing prayer about this, saying, well hello, that is the Holy Spirit who has placed a ministry, a burden of prayer, on your soul.

63
00:07:49.418 --> 00:07:57.418
To say, do you want to partner with me, the Son Jesus Christ, do you want to pray about this with me?

64
00:07:57.418 --> 00:08:09.418
To rest in that, to learn more about it. Read the Bible about it, learn it, talk about it, pray about it, you understand, that is a ministry.

65
00:08:09.418 --> 00:08:23.418
I know that one of the ministries I have, a ministry that I feel very strongly in my life, is that I want to explain Scripture to the world in the simplest way possible.

66
00:08:23.418 --> 00:08:41.418
That is really what I live for. I want to explain the Bible simply. Basic, Bible, stuff I want to explain to a generation in 2024, the Netherlands and Belgium.

67
00:08:41.418 --> 00:08:58.418
Let me explain what I mean, what occupies my mind. When I look around me, I see that the Netherlands and Belgium are no longer raised in a Christian way. It is becoming less and less a godly society in which we live.

68
00:08:58.418 --> 00:09:23.418
So some of the Christians sitting in this church, the children who have grown up in Christian families, that is no longer the norm of this pagan society in which we live. So you have a Christian society, where the legislation, the government, the culture, the way of doing things, are actually based on the norms and values of the Bible.

69
00:09:23.418 --> 00:09:41.418
Then you have a Christian culture. But as it says in Romans chapter 1, where Paul says, the more people reject God, the more God says, okay, if you reject me, then I will also give you over to your own foolishness.

70
00:09:41.418 --> 00:10:01.418
That is a logic. That is just logical. If you say, I don't need God, then God says, yes, but then you also don't have my blessing. And if a country does not have the blessing of God, then that country or that culture or that society is handed over to the godless culture in which it wishes to live. That is fair. Fair is fair.

71
00:10:01.418 --> 00:10:17.418
And so when I look around me, I see a pagan culture, where the norms and values of the Christian faith, listen carefully to what I say, are often still present in people, but they don't even know that it is built on the rock.

72
00:10:17.418 --> 00:10:35.418
Marriage is from Jesus. People are still getting married, thinking they are doing it for themselves, but it comes from Christ. Norms and values that were once based on Jesus, but it fades and it fades.

73
00:10:35.418 --> 00:10:49.418
And ultimately we are in the end times, we are in the last days, I want to say, wait, I have to say, the end times is a spooky word, we are in the last days, as Paul says.

74
00:10:49.418 --> 00:11:07.418
And what occupies me a lot, by reflecting on myself, is that I want to direct the teaching in open church so that everyone in the room can take clear steps in faith with Jesus.

75
00:11:07.418 --> 00:11:22.418
Simple, clear steps. Almost as if I would say, these are no-brainers, everyone understands this, but when I think about the pagan society in which we live, not everyone understands this.

76
00:11:22.418 --> 00:11:51.418
You understand? And that is why I find it important to explain the Bible decently, solidly, and basically. And what I want to give simple teaching about today are the Bible verses that are in a Christian, that a Christian can recall, easily throw up from the memories we have as Christians, because you read your Bible.

77
00:11:52.418 --> 00:12:06.418
And the title, if you are taking notes, the title I wrote down was very simple, thank you Lord for this meal. Thank you Lord for this meal.

78
00:12:07.418 --> 00:12:25.418
Here is the first assignment that I just want to give to the church. Dear church, brothers and sisters in faith, believers and followers of Jesus, be thankful to God at every meal you eat.

79
00:12:26.418 --> 00:12:41.418
And here, wow, can't you talk a bit more significantly? No, this is it. This is it. I want to convey to the church, church, thank God at every meal you eat. That's the lesson.

80
00:12:42.418 --> 00:12:54.418
Okay, why then? Because it is important for Christians to pause and appreciate how beautiful it is that God provides us with a meal.

81
00:12:55.418 --> 00:13:08.418
Do not live for yourself. Do not live quick, quick, quick. Do not see food as something you eat quickly, on the go, where I have cravings at that moment, every stimulus.

82
00:13:08.418 --> 00:13:20.418
I am not talking about a bag of Doritos. I am not talking about a can of Red Bull. I am not talking about a quick snack at the traffic light. I am talking about a decent meal that you put on the table.

83
00:13:20.418 --> 00:13:29.418
Dear church, pray for the food and thank the Lord. And let me elaborate on this.

84
00:13:30.418 --> 00:13:40.418
The Bible is a theological book. The Jews and also the Christians in the New Testament, but especially the Jews.

85
00:13:40.418 --> 00:13:52.418
The Jews were already engaged in writing their scriptures from the very first writings about the relationship between God and man.

86
00:13:52.418 --> 00:14:01.418
The Bible is a theological book. You can also see other tribes in the world throughout history.

87
00:14:01.418 --> 00:14:10.418
You have other cultures, you have other countries that valued different things since the invention of writing.

88
00:14:10.418 --> 00:14:18.418
You can go back thousands of years to another culture, and you will find writings in archaeology.

89
00:14:18.418 --> 00:14:26.418
And with those writings, you will read in that particular language, and all those professors and archaeologists do their best to decipher that.

90
00:14:26.418 --> 00:14:35.418
And then you can see, for example, that some cultures were primarily focused on writing about military victories.

91
00:14:35.418 --> 00:14:40.418
They found that very important. So what did they do? They wrote down military matters.

92
00:14:40.418 --> 00:14:46.418
And so all the writings you find about that culture are primarily military.

93
00:14:46.418 --> 00:14:52.418
Then you have another culture that found it very important to write down their inventions.

94
00:14:52.418 --> 00:14:55.418
And they mainly did that in science.

95
00:14:55.418 --> 00:15:02.418
Then you have, for example, the Greeks, who found it very important to talk about philosophy, wisdom.

96
00:15:02.418 --> 00:15:10.418
So different peoples have different theses, different subjects they wrote about.

97
00:15:10.418 --> 00:15:17.418
The Jews found one thing very important, and that is the relationship between God and man.

98
00:15:17.418 --> 00:15:21.418
That is why the Bible we have is a theological book.

99
00:15:21.418 --> 00:15:24.418
It is about God and man.

100
00:15:24.418 --> 00:15:28.418
It is about people, it is full of people, but it is mainly about Yahweh.

101
00:15:28.418 --> 00:15:33.418
It is mainly about the Creator, it is mainly about the King and His name is Jesus.

102
00:15:33.418 --> 00:15:35.418
Hallelujah, blessed is His name.

103
00:15:35.418 --> 00:15:37.418
And why am I explaining this?

104
00:15:37.418 --> 00:15:42.418
Because today I am going to talk about food, but I want to connect that to God.

105
00:15:42.418 --> 00:15:45.418
